        "uuid": "cae71339_f4becda4",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115178
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-14T20:03:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PathForModuleGen() provides that as a path within a modules\u0027 intermediates directory, so it seemed like a reasonable path to copy our generated sources to. I don\u0027t mind changing it to something else.\n\nManually pre-generated source that resides in a local source tree likely just needs to be checked into source, so the choice of path wouldn\u0027t impact that use case I think.\n\nccross@, is there some additional meaning to the path provided by PathForModuleGen() such that we should deconflict and use another path to copy generated source from dependencies to?",
      "parentUuid": "aa342a81_9a84c20a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "418910c10fdb200e33e9add41d03b44e42bb18bb",
